Adding a new dataset to VSLAM-LAB is now one CLAUDE skill:

claude skill add-dataset dataset_name url

Point it at a dataset page and CLAUDE writes the integration: download, extraction, rgb, intrinsics, ground truth, everything in the VSLAM-LAB format, ready for every system in the benchmark.

To put it to the test, I used it to integrate the NSAVP dataset (Novel Sensors for Autonomous Vehicle Perception), recorded by the University of Michigan on ~8 km driving routes through Ann Arbor under varied lighting conditions. NSAVP also ships stereo event and stereo thermal cameras.
🌐 Dataset: https://umautobots.github.io/nsavp

Then I ran AllFeature-VSLAM, tightly coupling ORB + ALIKED features, with two precomputed additions that make the difference on driving data:

🚫 Dynamic object removal with Mask2Former: points falling on cars, pedestrians and other movers are segmented out.

📏 Depth from stereo with FastFoundationStereo: every feature gets metric depth from the stereo pair at initialization, giving a metrically scaled trajectory from the first frame.

The whole experiment is fully reproducible with a small YAML file:

exp_allfeature-dev:
  Config: config_nsavp.yaml
  NumRuns: 1
  Parameters: {verbose: 1, segmentation: mask2former, mode: rgbd, depth: fastfoundationstereo}
  Module: allfeature-dev

